  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C appears to exert its biological effects through a shared pathway involving Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which acts as a target of multiple entities, including Oblonganoside C, NCI-H1734, and Glycogen synthase kinase-3 alpha. All three of these entities are ultimately targeted by Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which in turn targets mRNA interferase EndoA. The evidence suggests a mechanistic link between Oblonganoside C and EndoA, mediated through Ent-Gloeosteretriol, with varying levels of confidence in the direct interaction between Oblonganoside C and EndoA. The scores from the three paths indicate a consistent but not absolute relationship, likely due to the indirect nature of the pathway. The presence of multiple targets for Ent-Gloeosteretriol suggests a potential for pleiotropic effects, but the core mechanism remains the inhibition of mRNA interferase EndoA through the action of Ent-Gloeosteretriol. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Oblonganoside C may modulate EndoA activity, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
